{
 "command": "dialog-template",
 "notes": [
  "Feeds W8-18d (dialogs::native::{template, chrome}). Reflection over the internal types of the PhotoReview (Shell.Win32) assembly: DialogTemplate, DialogItem, DialogControlClass, DialogColors, DarkDialogChrome.",
  "Output per kind: build -> bytes_length, bytes_hex (only when the template is at most 4096 bytes), or threw (exception type name); class_name -> value (ushort), class_name (string or null), window_class_name (string); theme_for -> theme (string, may be empty, or null); color_ref -> value (uint); from_key -> found (bool) plus value, or threw; named_colors -> window, input, text, text_strong, text_secondary, warning (uint each); constants -> header_bytes, atom_marker.",
  "Input floats are the exact decimal of a C# float (r,g,b are narrowed with a float cast before the call). A repeat object stands for count identical items (id 1..count, style 0)."
 ],
